<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SAFRICA'S CFC YEAR SHARE LEAPS, DIV UP.</title>
<headline>SAFRICA'S CFC YEAR SHARE LEAPS, DIV UP.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended Dec 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)	 </p>
<p>    Headline shr (cts)    119.2	 vs 79.0</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     199.4	 vs 63.6</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 48.0	  vs 34.0 </p>
<p>    Attrib income	   19.78	 vs 6.31</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   26.41	 vs 10.40</p>
<p>    Tax			 2.08	  vs 2.37</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   0.51	  vs 1.07</p>
<p>Div payable April 25</p>
<p>on register April 18</p>
<p>Full name: Commercial Finance Company Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - South African investment trust CFC said that its</p>
<p>forecast for 1997 was for a further increase in earnings but at</p>
<p>a slower level than 1996 </p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
